2026-10-14 | Stage 7 -- Playwright E2E suite against the current single-file game | The regression contract was 100% unverified, so Part C would have rewired a working game with no net; three first-run problems: headless mode wanted the separate chrome-headless-shell binary, and two of my own assertions were wrong (the drift fill is #h-drift itself, not a child, and a boundingBox on the minimap measures its 1px border so 100px of canvas reads as 102) | Pointed the project at the full Chromium via channel:chromium (no extra download, same WebGL a player gets) and fixed both assertions, the second by asserting computed CSS width instead of a box. Also found the game reads e.code, so the legend's AZERTY Z is KeyW -- my spec had tested z and would have failed for my reason, not the game's. 27 specs green in 2.8 min, R-01..R-09 now COVERED | playwright.config.ts tsconfig.json e2e/serve.mjs e2e/game.spec.ts package.json .claude/DECISIONS.md .design-sync/NOTES.md
2026-10-14 | Stage 8 -- repackage the game as a Vite app under apps/game | Three problems, two of them caught by the E2E net: vite preview binds to localhost which resolves to ::1 here, so Playwright waiting on 127.0.0.1 timed out; and the port introduced mojibake across all the French copy, because the original index.html never declared a charset and had been relying on the server's header (GitHub Pages and the test server both send charset=utf-8; vite preview does not) | Extracted markup and script mechanically with byte-identical verification rather than transcribing 1207 lines; pinned both Vite servers to 127.0.0.1 with strictPort; added an explicit meta charset, which fixes a latent bug the original file always had. 27/27 E2E green against the production build, 341 unit tests still green | apps/game/{index.html,package.json,vite.config.js} apps/game/src/game.js index.html (deleted) playwright.config.ts packages/ui/src/styles/parity.test.ts
